course: dictionary
lesson: 5594
title: Lichen: Two Living Things Working Together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lichen is not one simple thing. It is two living things living together: a fungus and a tiny alga (or sometimes bacteria). They help each other, so each one makes the other's life easier. The alga makes food from sunlight, and the fungus gives shelter and holds water.
explain: Look for lichen on rocks, walls, tree bark and old gravestones. It grows in crusty, leafy or bushy patches. Context helps you here: «In winter they live on lichen, bark and buds.» The sentence tells you lichen is something an animal can eat, so it must be food that grows on things.
explain: Lichen grows very slowly, so a patch on a stone may be older than you are. Many kinds die where the air is dirty, which is why scientists use lichens to test the air. When you meet a new word, read the words around it and look for clues.
fact: Lichen is made of a fungus and an alga (or bacteria) living together.
fact: The alga makes food from sunlight, and the fungus gives shelter and holds water.
fact: Lichen grows very slowly, and it can live in harsh places such as the Arctic.
fact: Many kinds of lichen die where the air is polluted, so lots of lichens mean clean air.
fact: Litmus paper gets its dye from lichens, and the dye has been used for hundreds of years.
exercise: What is lichen made of? | Only rock and sand | Ice crystals | *A fungus and a tiny alga (or bacteria) living together | Moss and tree sap
exercise: «These are golden snub-nosed monkeys, and in winter they live on lichen, bark and buds.» What do the monkeys eat in winter? | *Lichen, bark and buds | Sweets from the farm | Grass from the sea | Carrots from a bag
exercise: Why do scientists use lichens to check air quality? | Lichens glow in the dark | Lichens only grow in the sea | *Many kinds die where the air is polluted | Lichens make the air hotter
test: «Litmus paper turns red in acid and blue in alkali; its dye comes from lichens.» Where does the dye in litmus paper come from? | Salt water | Rain | *Lichens | Sand
test: What does lichen mean? | A kind of tree | *A living thing that grows in crusty, leafy or bushy patches on rocks, walls and bark | A metal used for building | A type of cold rain
exam: Which place can lichen live in, even where it is very cold? | Pond water | Desert sand | A hot kitchen | *The Arctic
